    "content_md": "Ian Fike\nProduct Lead\nSan Francisco, CA | (206) 455-5217 | fike101@gmail.com | linkedin.com/in/ianfike\n\nProfessional Summary\nSenior Product Manager with 9+ years owning platforms, shared systems, and cross-product\nexperience layers across regulated healthcare and high-growth SaaS. At Livongo/Teladoc,\nowned the shared platform foundation — registration, user accounts, data pipeline, partner\nintegrations, internal tooling, and customer support tooling — that every consumer and\nenterprise product line was built on, in a HIPAA-regulated environment serving millions of\nmembers. Led complex migrations, platform-wide changes, and cross-team coordination; built\ninternal tooling that created leverage for go-to-market, finance, and operations; and partnered\nclosely with engineering on API design, identity, licensing, and workflow orchestration.\nComfortable with system-design tradeoffs, technical fluency in APIs and design systems, and\naligning engineers, clinicians, and executives on a shared roadmap.\n\nCore Competencies\n   ●​ Platform Product Management: shared systems, cross-product experience layers,\n      reliability, scalability, extensibility, complex migrations, platform-wide changes, system\n      design\n   ●​ Growth Infrastructure: onboarding, activation, account provisioning, licensing,\n      cross-product preferences, self-service experiences, funnel instrumentation, registration\n   ●​ Internal Tooling & Partner Enablement: admin dashboards, access controls,\n      configuration management, licensing and billing integrations, demo environments, GTM\n      tooling, support tooling\n   ●​ Technical Fluency: APIs, identity management, licensing systems, design systems,\n      feature flagging, workflow orchestration, data instrumentation\n   ●​ Healthcare & Regulated SaaS: HIPAA, SOC 2 awareness, EMR-adjacent integrations,\n      clinician-facing workflows, enterprise health system partners\n   ●​ Data & Analytics: A/B testing, cohort analysis, funnel optimization, onboarding\n      telemetry, operational reporting, Amplitude, Mixpanel, SQL\n   ●​ Leadership: staff-level cross-functional alignment across engineering, design, data,\n      clinical, and GTM; OKRs; PRDs; roadmap planning; agile\n\nProfessional Experience\nProduct Advisor, Product Lead & Product Designer\nIndependent Consultant — San Francisco, CA | 2021 – Present\n   ●​ Advised five early-stage startups across health tech, education, and SaaS on platform\n      foundations, onboarding and activation flows, and internal tooling that unblocked GTM\n      and operations teams.\n   ●​ Built and shipped production systems hands-on (TypeScript, Supabase Edge Functions,\n      Postgres, vanilla JS) — designed APIs, data models, identity flows, and feature flag\n      scaffolding; reinforced system-design fundamentals through direct engineering work.\n\f   ●​ Led product discovery, roadmap planning, and backlog management; defined MVPs and\n      platform primitives in both pre- and post-product-market-fit environments.\n   ●​ Wrote PRDs, system specs, experiment briefs, and KPI definitions; partnered with\n      engineering on API design, data instrumentation, and migration planning.\n   ●​ Established OKRs and scalable product processes for founders; supported fundraising\n      with platform and architecture narratives.\nSenior Product Manager, User Growth — Platform & Growth Infrastructure\nLivongo Health & Teladoc — Mountain View, CA | 2018 – 2021\n   ●​ Owned the shared platform surface behind Livongo’s multi-condition, multi-product\n      portfolio — registration, user accounts, data pipeline, partner integrations, internal\n      tools, and customer support tooling — the cross-product foundation every consumer\n      and enterprise product line was built on, serving a clinician- and member-facing surface\n      in a HIPAA-regulated environment.\n   ●​ Delivered 3 new commercial product lines on top of the shared platform across\n      consumer and enterprise channels without forking the foundation, supporting company\n      growth and retention goals through the Teladoc merger.\n   ●​ Led complex platform migrations and cross-team coordination across engineering,\n      design, data science, clinical, and GTM; increased development team velocity 28% by\n      reducing internal dependencies and consolidating shared services.\n   ●​ Owned onboarding and activation infrastructure end-to-end — moving from manual\n      configuration to self-service experiences — and drove a 12% increase in enrollment\n      through funnel instrumentation, A/B testing, and registration redesign.\n   ●​ Built internal partner tooling for customer support, care operations, and enterprise\n      account teams; reduced support interaction time and improved support team efficiency\n      by 34%, creating real leverage for operations and GTM.\n   ●​ Partnered with Data Science and Analytics to define onboarding telemetry, funnel\n      tracking, and operational reporting across the platform; instrumented end-to-end\n      member journey to inform roadmap and SLAs.\n   ●​ Aligned engineers, clinicians, executives, and enterprise health system partners on\n      platform tradeoffs, API contracts, and shared-system roadmaps.\n   ●​ Owned roadmap for growth experimentation, registration, user accounts, data pipeline,\n      partner integrations, internal tools, and customer support — the platform layer of the\n      company.\nProduct Designer, Member Experience — Design System & Clinical UX\nLivongo Health — Mountain View, CA | 2016 – 2018\n   ●​ Built and maintained Livongo’s design system and shared UI components, enabling\n      new product lines to integrate without one-off work and accelerating downstream product\n      development cycles.\n   ●​ Designed patient- and clinician-facing interfaces and connected-device flows aligned\n      with HIPAA and clinical regulatory requirements; partnered with engineering on system\n      behavior, edge cases, and accessibility.\n\f   ●​ Conducted user research, wireframing, prototyping, and usability testing for the diabetes\n      management product and connected device ecosystem; partnered with PM and\n      engineering on feature specifications.\nProduct Designer, Growth & Enterprise\nRemind — San Francisco, CA | 2015 – 2016\n   ●​ Designed and tested onboarding, activation, and monetization flows across mobile,\n      SMS, and web; partnered with product and marketing on growth experiments that\n      improved retention and conversion.\n   ●​ Built the MVP for the School Administrator dashboard — internal and partner-facing\n      tooling that became the foundation of Remind’s enterprise offering and a new GTM\n      motion.\n\nEducation\nUniversity of Washington — Bachelor of Design, Interaction Design | June 2015\n\nSkills & Technologies\n   ●​ Product Management: platform PM, shared systems, cross-product experience layers,\n      PRDs, MVP definition, roadmap planning, OKRs, agile, stakeholder alignment, complex\n      migrations\n   ●​ Growth & Onboarding: activation, registration, account provisioning, self-service flows,\n      A/B testing, cohort analysis, funnel optimization, user segmentation\n   ●​ Platform & Engineering Fluency: APIs, REST, identity management, licensing and\n      entitlements, design systems, feature flagging, workflow orchestration, system design,\n      data pipelines\n   ●​ Healthcare & Compliance: HIPAA, SOC 2 awareness, EMR-adjacent integrations,\n      regulated product development, clinician workflows\n   ●​ Data & Analytics: Amplitude, Mixpanel, Google Analytics, SQL, telemetry,\n      instrumentation, operational reporting\n   ●​ Tools: Jira, Figma, Confluence, Notion, Airtable, Linear, GitHub, Supabase, TypeScript,\n      Postgres\n\nCertifications & Recognition\nKleiner Perkins Design Fellow, 2015\nReforge Growth Series Graduate, 2019\nLivongo PROPEL Award Recipient\n\f",
