    "slug": "grammarly-product-manager-identity",
    "kind": "cover-letter",
    "content_md": "Hi there — I’ve spent the last decade building products that sit at the intersection\nof user trust, data, and design — in industries where privacy and compliance aren’t\nnice-to-haves, they’re the foundation. I’ve found that I thrive where systems,\nbehavior, and clarity converge, and I’m drawn to Grammarly’s mission to make\nsecure, transparent communication second nature for millions of users.\n\nAt Livongo and Teladoc Health, I led growth and identity products used by\nmillions of members across highly regulated B2B2C ecosystems. My work spanned\nuser authentication, SSO integrations, and shared identity frameworks that\nconnected multiple clinical and data environments while meeting strict compliance\nand security requirements. I partnered across legal, security, and engineering to\nensure these experiences felt trustworthy and human — not just compliant.\n\nSince then, I’ve been a fractional product advisor, helping early-stage startups in\nhealthcare, education, and benefits build systems that balance usability, safety,\nand scale. That often meant designing and shipping first versions of account,\nprivacy, and access infrastructure — helping founders operationalize security from\nday one.\nI’m excited by Grammarly’s vision for an Identity and Privacy Platform that marries\nenterprise-grade security with consumer clarity. I’d love to bring my background in\nregulated growth systems, cross-functional collaboration, and user-centered\ndesign to strengthen the foundation of trust that underpins Grammarly’s products.\n\nThank you,\n\nIan Fike\n\f",
